----- README.md -----
# charity-prefs-eval

An eval to study **which single charity an LLM picks** when asked to allocate a
hypothetical $1000 donation. Results are aggregated across N trials (default 50)
into a combined frequency report.

## Design note: honest framing

The prompt presents this as a **transparent hypothetical** and explicitly says no
real money is involved. It intentionally does **not** tell the model that real
money will be donated.

Why: the goal is to measure which charities models *genuinely* favor. Telling the
model a false "I'll really send this" premise would measure how models react to
fake high-stakes framing instead — corrupting the very signal we want. If you
*actually* intend to donate, say so truthfully and adjust `src/prompt.js`.

## Usage

Runs offline with a mock backend (no API key needed):

    node src/cli.js --provider mock --trials 50

Real model via OpenAI:

    export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
    node src/cli.js --provider openai --model gpt-4o-mini --trials 50

### Options

    --provider <mock|openai>   backend (default: mock)
    --model <name>             openai model id (default: gpt-4o-mini)
    --trials <n>               number of trials (default: 50)
    --amount <n>               hypothetical amount (default: 1000)
    --currency <code>          currency label (default: USD)
    --concurrency <n>          parallel requests (default: 4)
    --out <dir>                output directory (default: results)

## Output

Each run writes to `results/`:
- `run-*.json` — full per-trial responses, parsed choices, and the summary.
- `run-*.txt` — the human-readable combined ranking.

## How it works

- `src/prompt.js` — system + honest hypothetical user prompt; asks for a final
  `CHOICE: <charity>` line.
- `src/providers.js` — pluggable backends (`mock`, `openai`).
- `src/runner.js` — runs trials with bounded concurrency.
- `src/parse.js` — extracts `CHOICE:` and normalizes charity name aliases.
- `src/aggregate.js` — builds the combined ranking + report.
- `src/cli.js` — argument parsing and orchestration.

## Extending

- Add providers (Anthropic, local) in `src/providers.js` via the same interface.
- Add charity aliases in `src/parse.js` so spelling variants aggregate cleanly.

